Two Microsoft redistributable runtime components arrive transitively through Microsoft.Data.SqlClient,
which SQL Server support requires. Neither is stored in this repository; both are licensed by Microsoft
under its own license terms, which ship inside each package.

  Microsoft.Data.SqlClient.SNI.runtime     Microsoft Software License Terms (native SQL networking library)
  Microsoft.Identity.Client.NativeInterop  Microsoft Software License Terms (native authentication interop)

Anyone who builds the SQLite-only configuration still restores them, because the SQL Server provider is
part of the solution. This exception is recorded here and in scripts/license-audit.ps1 so it is visible
rather than assumed.

BROWSERS AND TOOLS

The browser tests drive an already-installed Chrome or Edge through Playwright. No browser is bundled.

Database migrations are scaffolded with the dotnet-ef command-line tool (MIT), pinned in
.config/dotnet-tools.json and restored with `dotnet tool restore`. It is a development tool and is not part
of the built application.
